The coalesced right injection relates a right neighbourhood Y to a coalesced neighbourhood W when the right injection of Y is contained in W. The master is related because the right injection of the right master lies under the coalesced master. If Y is the right master, both related codomain neighbourhoods equal the coalesced master, so their intersection does too; otherwise that intersection is a coalesced neighbourhood containing the injection. The relation is monotone because right injection preserves inclusion.
